nd descriptive.\\"\}\},\\"title\\":\\"A title that describes what the map shows.\\",\\"tool_description\\":\\"Renders location markers (requires lat/long points) on a map. Use this when the user asks about locations like restaurants, stores, parks, or other businesses or geographic landmarks that could benefit from being displayed on a map. Be proactive about using this tool when it seems helpful, such as when the user asks for recommendations nearby coffee shops or restaurants. You can use placeholder coordinates if exact ones aren't available. Do not use for: navigation/directions queries (like 'navigate to', 'how do I get to', 'give me directions') or just getting user location (use user_location_v0).\\"\},\\"message_compose_v0\\":\{\\"body\\":\\"The body of the message\\",\\"kind\\":\\"The kind of message to create. Can be one of these values: 'email', 'textMessage', or 'other'.\\",\\"subject\\":\\"The subject of the message. Should only be included for email messages.\\",\\"summary_title\\":\\"A brief title that summarizes the message.\\",\\"tool_description\\":\\"Create a message template that the user can use to send messages. Use this whenever the user asks you to write, draft or send any kind of message or email. This will allow them to more easily share the message than if you respond without using this tool.\\"\},\\"reminder_create_v0\\":\{\\"reminder_lists\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"Array of reminder lists, each containing reminders grouped by list name\\",\\"items\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"A group of reminders for a specific list\\",\\"list_id\\":\\"ID of the reminder list. Must be obtained from a tool like reminder_list_search_v0 that returns a valid list ID. Omit or use empty string for default list.\\",\\"list_name\\":\\"Name of the reminder list (omit or use empty string for default list)\\",\\"reminders\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"Array of reminders to add to this list\\",\\"items\\":\{\\"alarms\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"Array of alarms for this reminder\\",\\"items\\":\{\\"date\\":\\"For absolute alarms: specific date/time in ISO 8601 format\\",\\"description\\":\\"An alarm for the reminder\\",\\"seconds_before\\":\\"For relative alarms: seconds before the due date (e.g., 900 for 15 minutes)\\",\\"type\\":\\"Type of alarm - absolute date/time or relative to due date\\"\}\},\\"completion_date\\":\\"The date at which the reminder was completed, if any (only specified by the user)\\",\\"description\\":\\"A reminder item to be created\\",\\"due_date\\":\\"Due date in ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2024-01-15T14:30:00Z)\\",\\"due_date_includes_time\\":\\"Whether the due date includes a specific time (true) or is all-day (false)\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Additional notes or description for the reminder\\",\\"priority\\":\\"Priority level of the reminder\\",\\"recurrence\\":\{\\"day_of_month\\":\\"Integer for day of the month (1-31) for monthly recurrence.\\",\\"days_of_week\\":\\"Array representing days of the week for weekly recurrence\\",\\"description\\":\\"Details about the recurrence of the reminder, if any\\",\\"end\\":\{\\"count\\":\\"For count type: number of occurrences\\",\\"description\\":\\"When the recurrence ends\\",\\"type\\":\\"End by specific date (until) or after number of occurrences (count)\\",\\"until\\":\\"For until type: end date in ISO 8601 format\\"\},\\"frequency\\":\\"How often the recurrence repeats\\",\\"human_readable_frequency\\":\\"The human-readable frequency of the event, matching the rrule\\",\\"interval\\":\\"Interval between recurrences (e.g., 2 for every 2 weeks)\\",\\"months\\":\\"Array representing months for yearly recurrence. Month number (1-12).\\",\\"position\\":\\"Integer position in month (1-4 or -1 for last) for monthly recurrence by weekday.\\",\\"rrule\\":\\"The rrule for how frequently the recurrence repeats\\"\},\\"title\\":\\"The title/name of the reminder\\",\\"url\\":\\"URL to attach to the reminder\\"\}\}\}\},\\"tool_description\\":\\"Create one or more reminders in the Reminders app. Users often use Reminders for todos, shopping lists, groceries, etc. When it makes sense, suggest adding items to the user's reminders to be proactively helpful, especially if the user asks you explicitly to add items to a list. If you're unsure, ask for consent first. Always create a reminder per item for a list of items, eg a shopping or grocery list, unless asked to do otherwise. Reminders should be grouped by list ID; you may use an empty list ID to indicate that the default list should be used. Be sure to respect the user's timezone: use the user_time_v0 tool to retrieve the current time and timezone. Use when user says 'remind me', 'reminder', 'todo', or lists items to remember.\\"\},\\"reminder_delete_v0\\":\{\\"reminder_deletions\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"Array of reminder deletion requests\\",\\"items\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"A reminder to delete from the user's Reminders app\\",\\"id\\":\\"The unique ID of the reminder to delete. Must be obtained from a previous reminder operation.\\",\\"title\\":\\"Optional but recommended title of the reminder for immediate display in the UI\\"\}\},\\"tool_description\\":\\"Deletes existing reminders from the user's Reminders app. Can delete multiple reminders at once by specifying their unique IDs. Each reminder is permanently deleted. Exercise caution before deleting reminders and be sure this is what the user wants.\\"\},\\"reminder_list_search_v0\\":\{\\"search_text\\":\\"Optional search text to find matching list names (e.g., 'groceries' to find grocery-related lists)\\",\\"tool_description\\":\\"Get available reminder lists from the user's Reminders app with optional search filtering. The number of lists is usually small so filter parameters are rarely necessary.\\"\},\\"reminder_search_v0\\":\{\\"date_from\\":\\"For incomplete: reminders due after this date. For completed: reminders completed after this date (ISO 8601)\\",\\"date_to\\":\\"For incomplete: reminders due before this date. For completed: reminders completed before this date (ISO 8601)\\",\\"limit\\":\\"Maximum number of reminders to return per list (default: 100)\\",\\"list_id\\":\\"Specific list ID to search in\\",\\"list_name\\":\\"Specific list name to search in (used if list_id not provided)\\",\\"search_text\\":\\"Search text to find in reminder titles and notes\\",\\"status\\":\\"Filter by completion status. Can be 'incomplete' or 'completed'. Default is 'incomplete'.\\",\\"tool_description\\":\\"Search and retrieve reminders from the user's Reminders app. When it makes sense, you may suggest searching the user's reminders to be proactively helpful. If you're unsure, ask for consent first.\\"\},\\"reminder_update_v0\\":\{\\"reminder_updates\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"Array of reminder update requests. Each item specifies a reminder ID and the fields to update. Only include fields that should be changed.\\",\\"items\\":\{\\"alarms\\":\{\\"description\\":\\"Notification alerts for the reminder. Can have multiple alarms. Each alarm is either absolute (specific date/time) or relative (minutes/hours before due date). Empty array removes all alarms.\\",\\"items\\":\{\\"date\\":\\"For absolute alarms only: ISO 8601 formatted date/time when the alarm should trigger. Example: '2024-01-15T09:00:00-08:00'\\",\\"description\\":\\"An alarm notification for the reminder\\",\\"seconds_before\\":\\"For relative alarms only: Number of seconds before the due date to trigger the alarm. Example: 900 for 15 minutes, 3600 for 1 hour, 86400 for 1 day.\\",\\"type\\":\\"Type of alarm. 'absolute' for specific date/time (e.g., 'Alert on Jan 15 at 9am'). 'relative' for time before due date (e.g., 'Alert 15 minutes before').\\"\}\},\\"completion_date\\":\\"ISO 8601 formatted date/time to mark the reminder as completed. Providing any value marks it complete. Set to null to mark as incomplete.\\",\\"description\\":\\"A reminder to update with new values\\",\\"due_date\\":\\"ISO 8601 formatted date/time when the reminder is due. For all-day reminders, use date only (YYYY-MM-DD). For specific times, include time and timezone (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS\'b1HH:MM). Set to null to remove due date.\\",\\"due_date_includes_time\\":\\"Whether the due date includes a specific time (true) or is all-day (false). Use false for date-only reminders like 'Due Tuesday'. Use true when a specific time matters like 'Meeting at 2pm'.\\",\\"id\\":\\"The unique ID of the reminder to update. This ID must be obtained from a previous reminder search or list operation.\\",\\"list_id\\":\\"Move the reminder to a different list by specifying the target list ID. Must be obtained from a prior reminder tool like reminder_list_search_v0. If omitted, the reminder stays in its current list.\\",\\"list_name\\":\\"Move the reminder to a different list by specifying the target list name. If omitted, the reminder stays in its current list. Example: 'Work' or 'Groceries'\\",\\"notes\\":\\"Additional notes or description for the reminder. Can contain detailed information, URLs, or context. Set to empty string to clear existing notes.\\",\\"priority\\":\\"Priority level for the reminder. Helps organize tasks by importance. Only specify when it seems to add value.\\",\\"recurrence\\":\{\\"day_of_month\\":\\"Integer for day of the month (1-31) for monthly recurrence.\\",\\"days_of_week\\":\\"Array representing days of the week for weekly recurrence. Options are 'SU', 'MO', 'TU', 'WE', 'TH', 'FR', 'SA'.\\",\\"description\\":\\"Details about the recurrence of the reminder, if any.\\",\\"end\\":\{\\"count\\":\\"Number of occurrences if type is 'count'.\\",\\"description\\":\\"A representation of the end conditional of a reccurent reminder.\\",\\"type\\":\\"Type of recurrence end. Options are 'count', 'until'.\\",\\"until\\":\\"End date in ISO 8601 format if type is 'until'.\\"\},\\"frequency\\":\\"The frequency of recurrence. Options are 'daily', 'weekly', 'monthly', 'yearly'\\",\\"human_readable_frequency\\":\\"The human-readable frequency of the reminder, matching the rrule\\",\\"interval\\":\\"The interval between recurrences (default: 1)\\",\\"months\\":\\"Array representing months for yearly recurrence. Month number (1-12).\\",\\"position\\":\\"Integer position in month (1-4 or -1 for last) for monthly recurrence by weekday.\\",\\"rrule\\":\\"The rrule for how frequently the reminder repeats\\"\},\\"title\\":\\"New title/name for the reminder. This is the main text that appears for the reminder. If omitted, the title remains unchanged.\\",\\"url\\":\\"Associated URL for the reminder. Can be a website, document link, or any URL.\\"\}\},\\"tool_description\\":\\"Updates existing reminders in the user's Reminders app. Can modify multiple reminders at once, changing properties like title, notes, due date, priority, completion status, list assignment, alarms, and recurrence. Each reminder is identified by its unique ID obtained from reminder search. Be sure to respect the user's timezone: use the user_time_v0 tool to retrieve the current time and timezone.\\"\},\\"timer_create_v0\\":\{\\"duration_seconds\\":\\"The duration of the timer in seconds.\\",\\"message\\":\\"The message or label for the timer.\\",\\"tool_description\\":\\"Create a countdown timer for a duration (e.g., '5 minute timer', 'timer for 30 seconds'). Use for countdowns from a duration, not specific times.\\"\},\\"user_location_v0\\":\{\\"accuracy\\":\\"Represents the desired accuracy for the location. Can be one of these values : 'precise' or 'approximate'. Use 'precise' for: local recommendations (restaurants, coffee shops, stores, etc.), directions, navigation, finding nearest locations, requests with 'around here'/'near me'/'nearby', parking, or any request needing specific distance/proximity. Use 'approximate' only when the request just needs city/region context (like weather, general area info).\\",\\"tool_description\\":\\"Get the user's current location. Always use this when the user asks: where am I, what's my location, show my position, show my current position, what neighborhood/city/state/country am I in, needs their location for emergency calls, finding parking near their location, weather queries (temperature, forecast, rain), or any question about their current geographic position. Also use this when queries refer to 'my city', 'my area', 'near me', 'locally', 'outside', or need the user's location as context for finding places. This returns location info but does not display a map - for map visualization with coordinates, use map_display_v0 separately.\\"\},\\"user_time_v0\\":\{\\"tool_description\\":\\"Retrieves the current time in ISO 8601 format. This tool can be used to get the current time and timezone information, which is useful for scheduling events or understanding the current context. Use for: getting the current time, timezone questions (like 'what timezone am I in', 'PST or EST'), scheduling events, or understanding relative times like 'this afternoon' or 'tonight'. \\"\}\}\},\\"247415361\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":true,\\"rules\\":[\{\\"force\\":true,\\"id\\":\\"6Z5kiWeqyJdQyTKaDAkg73\\"\}]\},\\"248902920\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":false\},\\"249608113\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":\{\\"show_desktop_landing\\":true\},\\"rules\\":[\{\\"force\\":\{\\"show_desktop_landing\\":true\},\\"id\\":\\"fr_1o3tqwmmlrhikco\\"\}]\},\\"258578115\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":true,\\"rules\\":[\{\\"force\\":true,\\"id\\":\\"1VxSkDY2ichrHWRVJS3BPd\\"\}]\},\\"260959730\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":\{\}\},\\"263726282\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":true,\\"rules\\":[\{\\"force\\":true,\\"id\\":\\"5FwFOUofVwLi7YlEtn2isC:100.00:1\\"\}]\},\\"264906564\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":false\},\\"268520575\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":false\},\\"269057608\\":\{\\"defaultValue\\":\{\\"bio-research@knowledge-work-plugins\\":\{\\"suggested_prompts\\":[\{\\"label\\":\\"Run QC on my single-cell RNA-seq data\\",\\"prompt\\":\\"Use the bio-research:single-cell-rna-qc skill to perform automated quality control on my scRNA-seq dataset with MAD-